    "### Step 0B: Dependency Manager (Installer)\n",
    "\n",
    "**What?**\n",
    "Provides an interactive Graphical User Interface (GUI) to manage and install Python packages categorized by domain (e.g., NLP, Computer Vision, Time Series, Tree Boosting). The user can select the specific packages required for their specific use case and install them with a single click.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why?**\n",
    "Machine Learning ecosystems evolve rapidly, and different tasks require different heavy dependencies (like PyTorch or Transformers) which may clutter a standard environment. Instead of relying on a monolithic, heavy `requirements.txt` file, this cell enables \"a la carte\" installations. It also verifies if a library is already imported to avoid redundant downloads.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs:**\n",
    "- User selection of specific package groups from the UI.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs:**\n",
    "- Dynamically installed Python packages using `pip`.\n",
    "- Live logs indicating the success or failure of the installation.\n"
   ]
  },
