    "### Step 1B: Data Ingestion and Parsing (Loader)\n",
    "\n",
    "**What?**\n",
    "A universal data ingestion interface that physically loads data into the global pipeline state. It supports flat files (CSV, TSV, Parquet, JSON, Excel), relational databases (SQLite), complex structures (Images, NetworkX Graphs), textual batch datasets, and built-in toy datasets. It automatically parses the structure and generates a quick statistical preview.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why?**\n",
    "Data ingestion is often repetitive and prone to syntax errors. A standardized visual loader abstracts away the complexity of parsing functions (like `pd.read_csv(...)`). It guarantees that no matter the format, the data is properly ingested, initial missing value ratios are evaluated immediately, and the output is standardized for the next stages.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs:**\n",
    "- Local files (uploaded via UI), remote URLs, raw text from clipboard, or selected pre-built toy datasets.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs:**\n",
    "- Parsed data structures (e.g., pandas DataFrames, Graph objects, image matrices) stored in `state.data_raw`.\n",
    "- Automatically extrapolated preliminary metadata (data types, column counts, missing value alerts).\n"
   ]
