    "### Step 2: Business Context & Objective Alignment\n",
    "\n",
    "**What?**\n",
    "A bridge linking business requirements to mathematical representations. Here, the user defines the specific Machine Learning domain (e.g., Tabular Classification, NLP, Vision, Time Series), selects the main target variable (Y), and defines the ultimate business goal or metric to track (e.g., minimizing false positives vs. maximizing overall accuracy).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why?**\n",
    "An algorithm can be mathematically perfect but completely useless in the real world if it answers the wrong question. Defining the context early on restricts or unlocks specific, relevant tools in later steps, and ensures the model is ultimately optimized towards the correct operational objectives.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs:**\n",
    "- The loaded dataset (from `state.data_raw`).\n",
    "- User input specifying the target column, problem type, and domain.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs:**\n",
    "- `state.business_context`: A populated dictionary defining the target variable and constraints.\n",
    "- Trigger states for subsequent cells to adapt their UI automatically (e.g., hiding textual processing if the task is Image Classification).\n"
   ]
