    "### Step 3: Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
    "\n",
    "**What?**\n",
    "A highly interactive visual dashboard to systematically investigate the dataset’s statistics. It provides extensive charting tools: univariate distributions, bivariate scatter plots, multivariate correlation matrices, and even specialized visualizations for non-tabular data like Graph nodes or Text frequencies.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why?**\n",
    "\"Garbage in, garbage out\". Machine Learning algorithms only learn from what they are fed. EDA is critical for empirically diagnosing data anomalies (e.g., a person aged 300 years, heavy class imbalances, feature leakage) before feeding them to a model. The insights gathered here drive the decisions for cleaning and feature engineering.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs:**\n",
    "- The working dataset and business context target.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs:**\n",
    "- Real-time interactive charts (Histograms, KDE plots, Boxplots).\n",
    "- Deep insight into missing data distributions, correlations, and feature hierarchies.\n"
   ]
