    "### Step 3B: Advanced Feature Engineering Laboratory\n",
    "\n",
    "**What?**\n",
    "An interactive workbench dedicated to crafting new information out of existing variables. It offers tools for mathematical combinations (ratios, logarithms), textual extraction (regex parsing, domain extraction), temporal decomposition (extracting Year/Month from timestamps), and binning/discretization of continuous features.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why?**\n",
    "Feature engineering is widely considered the \"secret sauce\" of high-performing Machine Learning models. Algorithms often fail to automatically deduce non-explicit relationships (e.g., a client's relative seniority vs. their age). Manually constructing these cross-features can drastically and massively improve the final predictive accuracy.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs:**\n",
    "- The raw or preliminary dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs:**\n",
    "- Newly generated columns appended to the working DataFrame.\n",
    "- A tracked log of the exact transformations applied (saved in `state.history` for future reproducible deployments).\n"
   ]
