    "### Step 4: Data Remediation and Cleaning\n",
    "\n",
    "**What?**\n",
    "An assistance interface that combats \"missing value\" issues (NaN, Null, or predefined corrupted strings). It displays a status report for each column and automatically recommends tactics to repair the information mathematically (Mean, Median, sophisticated KNN imputation) or categorically.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why?**\n",
    "Except for certain tree-based algorithms (like XGBoost), the vast majority of classical model architectures crash instantly if they encounter a missing value, as they require dense numerical matrices. Data cleaning is not just about dropping rows; it is about artificially reconstituting missing reality via inference without skewing the overall data distribution.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs:**\n",
    "- The partially processed dataset containing missing or irregular values.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs:**\n",
    "- A remediated dataset free of structural gaps (`state.data_cleaned`).\n",
    "- Transformation logs recording exactly how each missing value was imputed.\n"
   ]
