    "### Step 5: Categorical Encoding & Outlier Neutralization\n",
    "\n",
    "**What?**\n",
    "This step translates human-readable text and categories into machine-readable numerical vectors (using methods like One-Hot, Ordinal, Label Encoding, TF-IDF). Simultaneously, it offers configurable constraints to manage statistical outliers (e.g., Clipping, Robust Scaling) to prevent extreme values from distorting the dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why?**\n",
    "Machine Learning models rely on geometric equations and probabilistic gradients. Raw text or textual categories cannot be processed mathematically until they are converted into numerical representations that preserve semantic distance. Furthermore, unchecked extreme outliers can shatter normalization, leading to heavily skewed weights and unstable learning in regression or neural network models.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs:**\n",
    "- The cleaned dataset with text or categorical columns, and columns with extreme variance.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs:**\n",
    "- A fully numerical, normalized, and encoded dataset (`state.data_encoded`).\n",
    "- Recorded encoding dictionaries allowing the exact transformations to be applied to future unobserved production data.\n"
   ]
