    "### Step 8: Compilation, Serialization, and Production (Exporter)\n",
    "\n",
    "**What?**\n",
    "Aggregates the entire transactional history (every click, choice, and transformation executed by the user during the interactive session) into deployment-ready assets. It generates the serialized binary weights of the trained models, consolidates the steps into a standalone autonomous Python script, and outputs an HTML execution report.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why?**\n",
    "By very nature, Jupyter Notebooks operate in dynamic, manual states—which are terrible for Continuous Integration pipelines and software production. To deliver the model into an actual product, server, or cloud interface, this interactive process must be automatically translated into robust, isolated code. This script ensures that the exact cleaning chains, encodings, and model inferences will behave perfectly in production without human intervention.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs:**\n",
    "- The complete `state` object, encompassing history, encodings, configurations, and trained models.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs:**\n",
    "- `exported_pipeline.py`: A reproducible, autonomous Python script mapping the start-to-finish pipeline.\n",
    "- `trained_models.pkl`: The serialized binary objects representing the machine's learned weights.\n",
    "- `execution_report.html`: An audit trail and documentation of everything accomplished.\n"
